@title INC-3302 postmortem
@subtitle Late nightly sales reports at Marrow Retail on 2026-10-06
@author Data Platform team, Owner
@date 2026-10-06

kpi Reports late | 8 h 40 min | due 03:00, sent 11:40 UTC | bad
kpi Store managers affected | 214 | empty or stale reports | bad
kpi Backfill time | 95 min | ran serially | neutral

# Summary
The point-of-sale vendor added a column named `tender_subtype` to the sales feed without notice. The ingestion job failed on the new column. The failure alert went to a retired channel, so nobody knew until a store manager asked why the report was empty.

No wrong numbers were published; reports were late, empty or stale.

# Timeline
All times UTC on 2026-10-06.
table = time,event; 01:15,Vendor deploys the schema change; 02:10,Ingestion job fails for the first time; 02:40,Retries exhausted; 03:00,"Reports miss their deadline, no alert"; 07:25,A store manager asks in #retail-ops why the report is empty; 07:50,Support pages the Data Platform on-call; 08:35,Cause identified; 09:20,Schema mapping patched; 10:05,Backfill starts; 11:40,Reports published

# Contributing factors
- The pipeline failure alert still routed to the retired channel #data-alerts-old.
- There was no schema contract check on vendor feeds.
- The backfill ran serially.

# What went well
- Once paged, the on-call found the cause in 45 minutes.
- No wrong numbers were published.

# Action items
table = action,owner,due; Route pipeline alerts to the on-call pager,Samuel Achterberg,2026-10-16; Require 14 days' notice of feed changes in the vendor contract,Vendor Management,2026-10-30; Add a schema contract check on vendor feeds,Lucia Fontaine,2026-11-06; Parallelize the backfill by partition,Data Platform on-call,2026-11-20
